# Pre-push quality gates

`pnpm check:push` (`scripts/pre-push-check.mjs`, also `.husky/pre-push`) runs lint/format/build/test for **directly changed** monitored packages, plus substreams SQL validation when those paths change.

**Agents:** follow [cloud-quality-gates.mdc](cloud-quality-gates.mdc) — run `check:push` in **cloud**, then push with `--no-verify` only after that gate is green. Do not thrash the laptop with a second full suite.

## When checks apply

Monitored packages under `packages/`:

- `@onsocial/rpc`, `@onsocial/text-card`, `@onsocial/sdk`, `@onsocial/ui`
- `onsocial-backend`, `onsocial-gateway`
- `@onsocial/pages`, `@onsocial/portal`, `@onsocial/app`

Substreams SQL (Docker + Postgres 16 in cloud):

- `indexers/substreams/**/*.sql`
- `indexers/substreams/scripts/validate_sql.sh`
- `indexers/substreams/tests/fixtures/**`

Diff base is `@{upstream}..HEAD`. Unrelated packages are skipped. Dependents expansion is **off** unless `PRE_PUSH_DEPENDENTS=1`.

Skip for docs-only, contract-only, or infra-only changes outside those paths (and outside substreams SQL). Contracts / relayer are separate.

## Commands

```bash
pnpm check:push
PRE_PUSH_DEPENDENTS=1 pnpm check:push   # after shared-lib changes
```

Substreams path runs `bash indexers/substreams/scripts/validate_sql.sh` (fresh schema + upgrade fixture). Prefer cloud for this.

## Before committing

Pre-commit: `lint-staged` on staged monitored-package files (prettier + eslint --fix) — keep this local; it is light.

## CI

Path-filtered workflows (portal, backend, gateway, pages, …) remain the merge safety net. Substreams CI runs the same SQL validation. Cloud `check:push` before push mirrors what husky would have run locally.
